     1	/**
     2	 * The customer a scenario is about, as the office knows them: their standing
     3	 * with the MHPCO at the moment a premium is quoted.
     4	 *
     5	 * Both facts here are the office's view of its relationship with this customer
     6	 * rather than of the items insured, so this is also where the office decides
     7	 * what that relationship entitles the customer to: whether they count as
     8	 * long-standing, and whether this contract is a follow-up. The rates those
     9	 * entitlements earn are the premium rules' business, in {@link PremiumPolicy}.
    10	 */
    11	public record Customer(int yearsWithMHPCO, int contractsAlreadyHeld) {
    12	
    13	    private static final int LOYALTY_YEARS = 2;
    14	
    15	    /**
    16	     * The office counts a customer as long-standing from 2 years of business
    17	     * with the MHPCO up; a newer customer earns no loyalty.
    18	     */
    19	    public boolean isLongStanding() {
    20	        return yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS;
    21	    }
    22	
    23	    /**
    24	     * Every contract after the customer's first is a follow-up, however long
    25	     * they have been with the office.
    26	     */
    27	    public boolean holdsFollowUpContract() {
    28	        return contractsAlreadyHeld > 0;
    29	    }
    30	}
